From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:15:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] perf: the IPU's IDCT sums only coefficients that are
 not zero; colour conversion and bit reads without branches

The reference IDCT left out of its sums the terms of zero coefficients and the rows that are all zero, keeping the order of the rest, so its output is the same to the bit; the sums run across x, which the compiler vectorizes. Colour conversion does a row of 16 pixels without branches into the output buffer. The bit reader's fast path is inline, with refilling and the FIFO tail out of line.

Intro movie on the Mac: IPU samples from 680 to about 540; all 100 sampled frames byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
